## Epic Title and Description

**Epic: Literature-Parity v1 — Reusable Cross-Project Baseline Validation Workflow**

When a project reimplements a method from a paper that publishes no code, the reimplementation silently diverges from the published method, confounding any downstream comparison. This epic ships a reusable, claim-tier-integrated workflow to establish and enforce that parity. The deliverable is: a skill-first protocol (5-phase blind reconstruction → adversarial refutation → graded verdict) driven by a declarative `parity.bth.toml` args file with zero per-project code; a mechanical X1 cap-lattice grader that computes PARITY/PARTIAL/FAIL from evidence without adjudication; F2 conclude-gate and F3 submit-gate enforcement that hard-blocks confirmatory campaigns from proceeding until parity is attested; and sprint-audit Signal 13 for cross-project detection. Validated on the Zeinaty 2026 reshuffle case (asr project), where the workflow caught a mechanism-nullifying defect that 3 sprints of unit tests had missed.

