## Epic-Level Acceptance Criteria (condensed — full Given/When/Then in spec doc)

| AC | What it tests |
|---|---|
| AC-01 | parity.bth.toml validator rejects missing required fields |
| AC-02 | parity.bth.toml validator passes on valid file |
| AC-03 | `compute_grade()` forces FAIL when `invariant_pass=False` |
| AC-04 | `compute_grade()` caps at PARTIAL for `ambiguity_load="load_bearing"` |
| AC-05 | `compute_grade()` returns PARITY on all-clear evidence |
| AC-06 | F2 conclude-gate downgrades confirmation campaign with uncontrolled reference_parity |
| AC-07 | F2 conclude-gate warns but does not downgrade exploration campaign |
| AC-08 | F2 conclude-gate passes through when parity is controlled |
| AC-09 | F3 submit-gate hard-blocks validation/production with uncontrolled reference_parity |
| AC-10 | F3 submit-gate is advisory-only for exploration tier |
| AC-11 | `attest-parity` binds a valid passing parity run and re-anchors claim SHA |
| AC-12 | `attest-parity` rejects a run with missing `parity_run_type` metadata |
| AC-13 | `attest-parity` on partial run sets `controlled-by-protocol` status |
| AC-14 | Signal 13 flags uncontrolled reference_parity in sprint-audit anomalies |
| AC-15 | `bth run --out` registers the SHA-anchored triple in `output_paths` |
| AC-16 | `SKILL.md` has the `## Validating a reimplemented baseline` section |
| AC-17 | `literature-parity/` subdir has all required phase templates and example files |
| AC-18 | `compute_grade()` caps at PARTIAL for `reproduction_rung="R2"` |
| AC-19 | `parity_validate.py` result JSON includes `parity_run_type='literature_parity'` |

